   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "The Bath House pub (Greene King). Ground floor is a navy-painted pub front (#2f3d4f) with pale pilasters. West to east: a wide multi-pane sash window, a green 'Food served daily' board, a door in a pilastered surround, then a wide 3-light sash window. The east end has a cellar hatch. 'THE BATH HOUSE' is in copper letters on the pale render band above. The hanging sign is on an iron bracket, with a lantern. The upper floor is pale grey-green render (jettied/overhanging), with a single sash at the west, a wide 3-light sash centre-east, and another sash toward the east. I could only see the upper floor obliquely and partly cut off, so the window count is uncertain. Only 2 storeys are visible under the roof, so I scaled them to the 9.8 m OSM eave height."
